body:
I applied the 4-line fix to a /tmp copy of the current daemon (NOT your file; work-tree vcodecd.c is still aab3345b18454b08, untouched) and ran your whole suite on the copy:

  bash /tmp/n2hw-V41/patchtree/gpu/hwcodec/daemon/test/run_tests.sh
  -> asan 271/271, o2 271/271, tsan 271/271
  -> selftest 20/20 twice, selftest blobs match
  -> real n2vhost: N2TEST IP-REAL PASS 18/18
  -> N2TEST IP PASS 833/833        (42.6 s)
  patched copy sha256: vcodecd.c d6fda73ef9cdd113af841033146581325c0c52d8ca238dd67cc40081c0e409de

Exact hunk that passed (read_sequence_header, after dma_alloc at :523):

 +	/* V41 resolves the bitstream handle in n2vc_dma; hw->dma_alloc() does not register it. */
 +	r = n2vc_dma_guest_register(hw, NULL, handle, pa, bytes, NULL);
 +	if (r == -EEXIST) {
 +		(void)n2vc_dma_guest_forget(hw, handle);
 +		r = n2vc_dma_guest_register(hw, NULL, handle, pa, bytes, NULL);
 +	}
 +	if (r != 0 && r != -ENOSYS) { (void)hw->dma_free(hw->ctx, handle); return r; }
  ...
 +	(void)n2vc_dma_guest_forget(hw, handle);   /* before dma_free, :538 */
 	(void)hw->dma_free(hw->ctx, handle);

-EEXIST is the reused-handle case (session_drop_handle/guest_forget already uses this pattern). -ENOSYS only exists in daemon/test/fake_vhost.c, so the unit configs stay green unchanged. The real registry in ap/n2vc_dma.c never returns -ENOSYS.

Caveat: t_real only exercises OPEN (18 checks), not the 2-frame flow the lead asked for. The registration behaviour itself is proven in my suite: without register -> -EINVAL and no message; with it -> bytes=29, enc_bsaddr==pa, enc_bsva==0x80000000|handle (t_v41.c:1494, N2TEST V41 PASS 667/667). The real 2-frame check still needs your real-vhost run with seq_hdr_mode=0 as the lead requested. Nothing on the phone, nothing published; the copy is under /tmp only.
